The  driver  provides measurements from the SHT30/SHT31/SHT35 hu‐
midity/temperature sensors via the framework.  The  argument  se‐
lects the address at the bus.  The mode of operation, repeatabil‐
ity,  heater  controls, periodic update rate and crc validity can
be changed through nodes.  The following variables are  provided:
Lists the modes supported by the driver and chip.  Set the opera‐
tion  mode  of the chip.  The SHT3X chip can run in a single‐shot
measurement mode or a periodic  update  mode.   Use  one  of  the
strings listed in List the periodic update rates supported by the
driver  and  chip.  Set the periodic update rate when the mode of
operation is set to periodic.  The unit for this is  measurements
per  second,  or  ART  which is a mode that operates at an update
rate of 4Hz higher response time.  Use one of the strings  listed
in  Since  it is possible to have subsecond periodic updates from
the chip if so desired a device file is provided that can be used
to get the raw temperature and humidity  values  outside  of  the
framework.   The  structure of this output is the raw temperature
plus an 8‐bit CRC followed by the raw humidity plus an 8‐bit CRC.
